0,Orya-Tor languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orya–Tor_languages,"Stephen Wurm (1975) linked Orya and the Tor languages with the Lakes Plain languages, forming a branch of his Trans-New Guinea phylum. Clouse (1997) found no evidence of such a connection. [1] Malcolm Ross (2005) linked them instead with part of another erstwhile branch of TNG in a Tor-Kwerba proposal, and Usher makes a broadly similar ...",Kwinsu,Tor-Kwerba
1,Foja Range languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foja_Range_languages,"The Foja Range languages, or Tor-Kwerba in more limited scope, are a family of about two dozen Papuan languages. They are named after the Foja Mountains of western New Guinea.",Kwinsu,Tor-Kwerba
