7,Kwinsu in Indonesia people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/18953,"Introduction / History The Kwinsu people live in Papua Province, Indonesia, primarily in the mountainous interior near the headwaters of the Mamberamo River. They speak the Kwinsu language, which belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family. Historically, the Kwinsu have been an isolated group, dwelling in rugged terrain and dense forests. Their culture developed around clan-based social ...",Kwinsu,Tor-Kwerba
